  "reason": "The current best (config_031: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, acc=0.678) has only been tested with resnet50 as the image encoder. The image encoder dimension is completely unexplored in the multimodal setting—image-only resnet50 scored very low (0.208), but in a fused model the image may provide complementary signal that a stronger encoder like ViT-L could better capture. config_037 is a clean single-variable extension of the best config (only image encoder changes from resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l), so any performance difference is directly attributable to encoder quality. This is the highest-information next step: if ViT-L improves performance, it identifies image encoder strength as a productive axis for further gains; if it does not, it confirms the image modality's contribution is encoder-independent and redirects effort toward RNA encoder or aggregation choices. Under a limited budget, resolving this unexplored binary question is more valuable than testing a second RNA encoder (scgpt) or re-testing aggregation, both of which have weaker expected information gain given the strong existing evidence."
